{"conjecture": "Software systems accumulate a graph of implicit invariants—unstated relationships between components that emerge from the interaction of many individually correct changes. Each change optimizes locally against the *explicit* contract, but shifts the *implicit* invariant graph, so future developers must reverse-engineer an ever-growing web of undocumented constraints before making safe modifications. The difficulty grows super-linearly because the invariant graph is combinatorial in the number of component interactions, not linear in code size."}
